1.Remote state file ->
                    A remote state file means the Terraform state (terraform.tfstate) is 
                    stored in a remote location instead of on your local computer.

2.problem if state file is stored in local ->
                            Different copies of the state.
                            Conflicting changes.
                            Difficult to collaborate.
                            Risk of losing the state if a laptop fails.

3.Remote state with state locking ->
                            A remote state file is a Terraform state file stored in a shared 
                            backend (such as Amazon S3) instead of on a local machine. 
                            It enables collaboration, provides a single source of truth for 
                            infrastructure state, and is commonly combined with state locking
                             to prevent concurrent modifications.